Herbert Broom, in his celebrated publication, A Selection of Legal Maxims has elaborated the essence thereof as hereunder:
"This phrase is based on the implied agreement of every member of the society that his own individual welfare shall, in cases of necessity, yield to that of the community;
and that his property, liberty and life shall, under certain circumstances, be placed in jeopardy or even sacrificed for the public good."

